[{"category":"section","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.jl","page":"Guide and API","text":"LlingLlang.jl builds and lazily composes weighted finite-state transducers and lets Julia applications provide custom immutable transducers and weight semirings through Vinary Tree's versioned resource ABI. It also consumes host-defined lattice values published by LLattice.jl. Start with the package README for ownership, concurrency, security, and complete examples.","title":"LlingLlang.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"index.html#Build-a-typed-scalar-WFST","page":"Guide and API","text":"WfstBuilder{Label,Weight} accepts the three family label carriers (UInt8, Char, and UInt64) and seven checked scalar-weight types. The default WfstBuilder() is the familiar Unicode/tropical specialization.\n\nusing LlingLlang\n\nbuilder = WfstBuilder{UInt64,CountWeight}(size_hint=2)\nsource = add_state!(builder)\ntarget = add_state!(builder)\nset_start!(builder, source)\nset_final!(builder, target, CountWeight(3))\nadd_arc!(builder, source, UInt64(10), UInt64(20), target, CountWeight(2))\ngraph = build!(builder)\n\narc = only(arcs(graph, source))\n@assert arc isa WfstArc{UInt64,CountWeight}\n@assert state(graph, target).final_weight == CountWeight(3)\nclose(graph)\n\nTropicalWeight, LogWeight, ProbabilityWeight, ArcticWeight, SignedTropicalWeight, CountWeight, and BooleanWeight reject values outside their ABI carriers at construction. Native composition requires equal label and weight types and applies that weight domain's path multiplication.\n\nFor named byte or UInt64 vocabularies, attach input/output SymbolTables to the builder. Tables assign dense labels and freeze with the graph. For lazy custom automata, subtype AbstractWfstProvider, return matching ProviderState{Label,Weight} values, then call provider(Label, Weight, implementation). The Rust engine captures and caches those states without cloning the automaton algorithm into Julia.\n\nEvery returned Wfst owns one family-resource retain. Call close deterministically; finalizers exist only as leak-safety fallbacks. resource creates an independent retain, while compose captures one immutable snapshot of each operand.","title":"Build a typed scalar WFST"},{"category":"section","location":"index.html#Consume-a-host-defined-lattice","page":"Guide and API","text":"LLattice.jl owns the provider implementation; DynamicLatticeValue is lling-llang's checked consumer. Import takes an independent retain, and every join, meet, or fold produces another independently owned value.\n\nusing LlingLlang\nimport LLattice\n\nencode(value) = Vector{UInt8}(codeunits(string(value.value)))\nhosts = [LLattice.provider(LLattice.MaxMin(value);\n    domain_id=\"demo.maxmin.v1..\", encode=encode) for value in (2, 7, 4)]\nvalues = [dynamic_lattice_value(host.resource) for host in hosts]\nclose.(hosts)\n\nmaximum = lattice_join_many(values[1], values[2:3])\nminimum = lattice_meet(values[1], values[2])\n@assert String(lattice_stable_bytes(maximum)) == \"7\"\n@assert String(lattice_stable_bytes(minimum)) == \"2\"\nvalidate_lattice_laws(values)\n\nclose(maximum); close(minimum); close.(values)\n\nThe 16-byte domain identifier names both the encoding and the algebra. Values from different domains are rejected before a foreign callback runs. Law validation checks representative samples and can falsify, but not prove, the universal lattice laws. Julia handles are same-thread consumers; the Rust adapter uses fail-fast atomic admission and does not hold a mutex while host code executes.","title":"Consume a host-defined lattice"},{"category":"section","location":"index.html#Public-API","page":"Guide and API","text":"","title":"Public API"},{"category":"constant","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.ABI_VERSION","page":"Guide and API","text":"Native lling-llang ABI version required by this facade.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.ABI_VERSION"},{"category":"constant","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.API_REVISION","page":"Guide and API","text":"Minimum additive lling-llang API revision required by this facade.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.API_REVISION"},{"category":"type","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.AbiV2Header","page":"Guide and API","text":"Common fixed-layout prefix carried by every typed ABI-v2 structure.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.AbiV2Header"},{"category":"type","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.AbstractScalarWeight","page":"Guide and API","text":"Marker for an isbits Julia value in one built-in scalar semiring.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.AbstractScalarWeight"},{"category":"type","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.AbstractSemiringProvider","page":"Guide and API","text":"Implement the semiring operations below to publish a Julia weight algebra.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.AbstractSemiringProvider"},{"category":"type","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.AbstractWfstProvider","page":"Guide and API","text":"Implement wfst_start, wfst_state_count, and wfst_state for this type.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.AbstractWfstProvider"},{"category":"type","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.ArcticWeight","page":"Guide and API","text":"A max-plus scalar weight; finite values and -Inf are representable.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.ArcticWeight"},{"category":"type","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.BooleanWeight","page":"Guide and API","text":"A reachability weight encoded as exactly zero or one on the ABI wire.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.BooleanWeight"},{"category":"type","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.BudgetV2","page":"Guide and API","text":"Canonical state, arc, byte, and abstract-work limits.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.BudgetV2"},{"category":"type","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.CancellationV2","page":"Guide and API","text":"Thread-safe, first-reason-wins cooperative-cancellation owner.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.CancellationV2"},{"category":"type","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.CountWeight","page":"Guide and API","text":"An exact path count representable in the family ABI's Float64 slot.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.CountWeight"},{"category":"type","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.Digest256","page":"Guide and API","text":"A fixed-width evidence-context digest; all-zero bytes mean absent.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.Digest256"},{"category":"type","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.DynamicLatticeValue","page":"Guide and API","text":"Owned native adapter for one immutable host-defined lattice value.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.DynamicLatticeValue"},{"category":"type","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.Id128","page":"Guide and API","text":"A fixed-width semantic identifier; all-zero bytes mean absent.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.Id128"},{"category":"type","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.LogWeight","page":"Guide and API","text":"A negative-log scalar weight; finite values and Inf are representable.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.LogWeight"},{"category":"type","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.NativeError","page":"Guide and API","text":"A copied native error with its stable status and thread-local diagnostic.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.NativeError"},{"category":"type","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.OutcomeV2","page":"Guide and API","text":"Orthogonal semantic, completion, publication, and evidence outcome axes.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.OutcomeV2"},{"category":"type","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.ProbabilityWeight","page":"Guide and API","text":"A nonnegative finite scalar weight with sum/product operations.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.ProbabilityWeight"},{"category":"type","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.ProviderArc","page":"Guide and API","text":"One type-stable provider arc. nothing denotes epsilon on either tape.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.ProviderArc"},{"category":"type","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.ProviderState","page":"Guide and API","text":"One immutable state returned by a host provider.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.ProviderState"},{"category":"type","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.SemiringContext","page":"Guide and API","text":"Owned native adapter for one host-defined semiring operation context.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.SemiringContext"},{"category":"type","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.SemiringWeight","page":"Guide and API","text":"One owned dynamic weight scoped to its exact SemiringContext.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.SemiringWeight"},{"category":"type","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.SignedTropicalWeight","page":"Guide and API","text":"A signed min-plus scalar weight; finite values and Inf are representable.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.SignedTropicalWeight"},{"category":"type","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.Status","page":"Guide and API","text":"Stable status returned by the lling-llang C ABI.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.Status"},{"category":"type","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.SymbolTable","page":"Guide and API","text":"A dense, optionally frozen vocabulary mapping strings to byte or u64 labels.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.SymbolTable"},{"category":"type","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.TropicalWeight","page":"Guide and API","text":"A min-plus scalar weight; finite values and Inf are representable.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.TropicalWeight"},{"category":"type","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.Wfst","page":"Guide and API","text":"Immutable type-stable view over one retained scalar-WFST resource.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.Wfst"},{"category":"type","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.WfstArc","page":"Guide and API","text":"One type-stable immutable arc decoded from the family ABI.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.WfstArc"},{"category":"type","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.WfstBuilder","page":"Guide and API","text":"Mutable builder parameterized by label and built-in scalar-weight types.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.WfstBuilder"},{"category":"type","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.WfstDescriptorV2","page":"Guide and API","text":"Replay-critical tape, algebra, snapshot, and evidence-context identity.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.WfstDescriptorV2"},{"category":"type","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.WfstState","page":"Guide and API","text":"A type-stable state snapshot with its outgoing arcs.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.WfstState"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.abi_version-Tuple{}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Return the ABI version exported by the loaded native library.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.abi_version"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.acceptor_intersect-Union{Tuple{W}, Tuple{L}, Tuple{Wfst{L, W}, Wfst{L, W}}} where {L, W}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Weighted intersection of verified scalar acceptors under a required four-axis budget.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.acceptor_intersect"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.add_arc!-Union{Tuple{W}, Tuple{L}, Tuple{WfstBuilder{L, W}, Integer, Any, Any, Integer}, Tuple{WfstBuilder{L, W}, Integer, Any, Any, Integer, Any}} where {L, W}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Append an arc from from to target.\n\nLabels use the builder's UInt8, Char, or UInt64 domain; strings are interned through the corresponding tape's symbol table. nothing is epsilon. The default weight is the selected semiring's multiplicative identity.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.add_arc!"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.add_state!-Tuple{WfstBuilder}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Append one state and return its zero-based identifier.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.add_state!"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.api_revision-Tuple{}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Return the additive API revision exported by the loaded native library.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.api_revision"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.arcs-Union{Tuple{W}, Tuple{L}, Tuple{Wfst{L, W}, Integer}} where {L, W}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Return type-stable outgoing arcs for state, preserving epsilon as nothing.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.arcs"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.build!-Union{Tuple{WfstBuilder{L, W}}, Tuple{W}, Tuple{L}} where {L, W}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Consume builder and return its immutable interoperable WFST.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.build!"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.clear_final!-Tuple{WfstBuilder, Integer}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Remove finality and its weight from state.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.clear_final!"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.close!-Tuple{WfstBuilder}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Release an unconsumed builder; repeated calls are harmless.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.close!"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.closure-Union{Tuple{Wfst{L, W}}, Tuple{W}, Tuple{L}} where {L, W}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Lazily accept zero or more repetitions of a weighted graph.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.closure"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.closure_plus-Union{Tuple{Wfst{L, W}}, Tuple{W}, Tuple{L}} where {L, W}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Lazily accept one or more repetitions, including empty when the input does.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.closure_plus"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.compose-Union{Tuple{W}, Tuple{L}, Tuple{VinaryTreeInterop.Wfst, Wfst{L, W}}} where {L, W}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Compose a raw VinaryTreeInterop WFST with a typed lling-llang WFST.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.compose"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.compose-Union{Tuple{W}, Tuple{L}, Tuple{Wfst{L, W}, VinaryTreeInterop.Wfst}} where {L, W}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Compose a typed lling-llang WFST with a raw VinaryTreeInterop WFST.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.compose"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.compose-Union{Tuple{W}, Tuple{L}, Tuple{Wfst{L, W}, Wfst{L, W}}} where {L, W}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Lazily compose snapshots of two domain-compatible scalar WFST resources.\n\nThe product joins the first output tape to the second input tape and combines matching weights with the declared built-in semiring's multiplication.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.compose"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.concat-Union{Tuple{W}, Tuple{L}, Tuple{Wfst{L, W}, Wfst{L, W}}} where {L, W}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Lazily accept paths from the first graph followed by the second.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.concat"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.connect-Union{Tuple{Wfst{L, W}}, Tuple{W}, Tuple{L}} where {L, W}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Materialize native connect/trim within a required four-axis budget.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.connect"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.determinize-Union{Tuple{Wfst{L, W}}, Tuple{W}, Tuple{L}} where {L, W}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Materialize native determinization within a required four-axis budget.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.determinize"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.dynamic_lattice_value-Tuple{VinaryTreeInterop.Resource}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Retain and validate a vt.lattice.val.1 resource through lling-llang.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.dynamic_lattice_value"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.freeze!-Tuple{SymbolTable}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Prevent future symbols from being interned and return table.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.freeze!"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.import_wfst-Union{Tuple{W}, Tuple{L}, Tuple{Type{L}, Type{W}, Union{VinaryTreeInterop.Resource, VinaryTreeInterop.Wfst, Wfst}}} where {L, W<:AbstractScalarWeight}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Copy a compatible immutable resource into a native lling-llang WFST.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.import_wfst"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.input_symbols-Tuple{Wfst}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Return the frozen input-tape symbol table, or nothing for raw labels.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.input_symbols"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.intern!-Union{Tuple{L}, Tuple{SymbolTable{L}, AbstractString}} where L","page":"Guide and API","text":"Return value's dense label, inserting it unless table is frozen.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.intern!"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.isfrozen-Tuple{SymbolTable}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Return whether table refuses new symbols.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.isfrozen"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.label-Tuple{SymbolTable, AbstractString}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Return the existing dense label for value, or throw KeyError.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.label"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.lattice_diagnostic-Tuple{DynamicLatticeValue}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Return the provider's advisory diagnostic string.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.lattice_diagnostic"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.lattice_domain_id-Tuple{DynamicLatticeValue}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Return the stable provider-defined domain identifier.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.lattice_domain_id"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.lattice_equal-Tuple{DynamicLatticeValue, DynamicLatticeValue}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Compare two same-domain dynamic values for exact semantic equality.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.lattice_equal"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.lattice_flags-Tuple{DynamicLatticeValue}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Return the provider's validated lattice capability flags.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.lattice_flags"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.lattice_join-Tuple{DynamicLatticeValue, DynamicLatticeValue}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Return the least upper bound of two same-domain dynamic values.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.lattice_join"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.lattice_join_many-Tuple{DynamicLatticeValue, AbstractVector{DynamicLatticeValue}}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Fold joins through the provider's bounded batch path when available.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.lattice_join_many"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.lattice_meet-Tuple{DynamicLatticeValue, DynamicLatticeValue}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Return the greatest lower bound of two same-domain dynamic values.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.lattice_meet"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.lattice_meet_many-Tuple{DynamicLatticeValue, AbstractVector{DynamicLatticeValue}}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Fold meets through the provider's bounded batch path when available.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.lattice_meet_many"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.lattice_stable_bytes-Tuple{DynamicLatticeValue}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Return the provider's canonical encoding for a dynamic lattice value.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.lattice_stable_bytes"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.minimize-Union{Tuple{Wfst{L, W}}, Tuple{W}, Tuple{L}} where {L, W}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Materialize native minimization of a deterministic graph within a required budget.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.minimize"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.output_symbols-Tuple{Wfst}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Return the frozen output-tape symbol table, or nothing for raw labels.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.output_symbols"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.project_input-Union{Tuple{Wfst{L, W}}, Tuple{W}, Tuple{L}} where {L, W}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Lazily keep input labels on both tapes; budget bounds input and potential output.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.project_input"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.project_output-Union{Tuple{Wfst{L, W}}, Tuple{W}, Tuple{L}} where {L, W}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Lazily keep output labels on both tapes; budget bounds input and potential output.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.project_output"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.provider-Union{Tuple{P}, Tuple{W}, Tuple{L}, Tuple{Type{L}, Type{W}, P}} where {L, W<:AbstractScalarWeight, P<:AbstractWfstProvider}","page":"Guide and API","text":"provider(Label, Weight, implementation; parallel=false, acyclic=false,\n         input_symbols=nothing, output_symbols=nothing)\n\nExpose an immutable Julia AbstractWfstProvider through vt.scalar-wfst.1. State callbacks are cached once per state. Customer code never executes while the facade holds its cache lock. Set parallel=true only when the provider is safe for concurrent and reentrant calls.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.provider"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.remove_epsilon-Union{Tuple{Wfst{L, W}}, Tuple{W}, Tuple{L}} where {L, W}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Materialize native epsilon removal within a required four-axis budget.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.remove_epsilon"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.reserve_states!-Tuple{WfstBuilder, Integer}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Reserve capacity for additional states without changing the graph.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.reserve_states!"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.resource-Tuple{VinaryTreeInterop.Wfst}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Return one independent retained resource for a WFST.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.resource"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.semiring_approx_equal-Tuple{SemiringContext, SemiringWeight, SemiringWeight, Real}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Return provider-defined approximate equality at epsilon.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.semiring_approx_equal"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.semiring_context-Tuple{VinaryTreeInterop.Resource}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Retain and validate a vt.semiring.*1 resource through native lling-llang.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.semiring_context"},{"category":"function","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.semiring_diagnostic","page":"Guide and API","text":"Return the provider's advisory diagnostic for a weight or its domain.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.semiring_diagnostic"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.semiring_equal-Tuple{SemiringContext, SemiringWeight, SemiringWeight}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Return exact semantic equality.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.semiring_equal"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.semiring_one-Tuple{SemiringContext}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Construct the multiplicative identity.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.semiring_one"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.semiring_plus-Tuple{SemiringContext, SemiringWeight, SemiringWeight}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Add two weights in their exact shared context.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.semiring_plus"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.semiring_plus_many-Tuple{SemiringContext, AbstractVector{SemiringWeight}}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Fold addition through the bounded provider batch path when available.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.semiring_plus_many"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.semiring_properties-Tuple{SemiringContext}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Return the provider's declared algebraic-property bitset.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.semiring_properties"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.semiring_provider-Tuple{AbstractSemiringProvider}","page":"Guide and API","text":"semiring_provider(implementation; domain_id, division=false, star=false,\n                  numeric=false, stable_bytes=false, batch=true,\n                  parallel=false, thread_bound=true)\n\nPublish arbitrary Julia weights through the host-semiring capability ABI. Tokens use a recycling, generation-checked arena, and Julia methods run without the arena lock. parallel=true is opt-in and incompatible with thread_bound. Optional vtables are exposed only when explicitly enabled.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.semiring_provider"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.semiring_stable_bytes-Tuple{SemiringContext, SemiringWeight}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Return the provider's canonical encoding for one weight.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.semiring_stable_bytes"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.semiring_times-Tuple{SemiringContext, SemiringWeight, SemiringWeight}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Multiply two weights in their exact shared context.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.semiring_times"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.semiring_times_many-Tuple{SemiringContext, AbstractVector{SemiringWeight}}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Fold multiplication through the bounded provider batch path when available.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.semiring_times_many"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.semiring_zero-Tuple{SemiringContext}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Construct the additive identity.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.semiring_zero"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.set_final!-Union{Tuple{W}, Tuple{L}, Tuple{WfstBuilder{L, W}, Integer}, Tuple{WfstBuilder{L, W}, Integer, Any}} where {L, W}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Mark state final with a value from the builder's scalar semiring.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.set_final!"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.set_start!-Tuple{WfstBuilder, Integer}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Set the builder's start-state identifier.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.set_start!"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.state-Union{Tuple{W}, Tuple{L}, Tuple{Wfst{L, W}, Integer}} where {L, W}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Return a type-stable state snapshot, or nothing for an unknown ID.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.state"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.symbol-Union{Tuple{L}, Tuple{SymbolTable{L}, L}} where L","page":"Guide and API","text":"Return the symbol assigned to a dense label, or throw KeyError.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.symbol"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.validate_lattice_laws-Tuple{AbstractVector{DynamicLatticeValue}}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Probe all lattice laws over at most sixteen representative values.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.validate_lattice_laws"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.wfst_start-Tuple{AbstractWfstProvider}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Return a provider's non-negative start-state identifier.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.wfst_start"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.wfst_state-Tuple{AbstractWfstProvider, UInt64}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Expand state into one complete immutable ProviderState.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.wfst_state"},{"category":"method","location":"index.html#LlingLlang.wfst_state_count-Tuple{AbstractWfstProvider}","page":"Guide and API","text":"Return the provider's state count, or nothing when it is not known.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LlingLlang.wfst_state_count"}]
